 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519712,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Maureen invests $5,000 in a bond with a maturity date in 5 years at a fixed coupon rate of 4.75%. What is Maureen’s return on investment?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "23.75%"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Each year, Maureen was paid 4.75% of the $5,000 she invested.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"part = percent \\times total\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"part = \\left( {0.0475} \\right)\\left( {5,000} \\right){\\text{  =  \\$237}}{\\text{.50}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Maureen is paid interest each year for five years.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5\\left( {237.50} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}\\$1,187.50\"></span></p>\n<p>The return on investment (ROI) is the percent difference between the initial investment (<i>P</i>) and the final value of the investment (<i>FV</i>), or <span data-math=\"{\\rm{ROI}} = \\frac{{FV - P}}{P}\"></span>, expressed as a percentage. The length of time of the investment is not considered in ROI.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{ROI}} =  \\frac{{1,187.50}}{{5,000}} = 0.02375 = 23.75\\% \"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
